00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:43.380
Yeah. I think one of the, the hardest things that this game was like had to acknowledge is like

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:51.240
just turning. And it, it's funny because most of us have, if we're playing a racing game, we're probably

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:57.080
playing a game that was released after the analog stick was invented, which allows you

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:03.440
to turn to a certain degree and not always just go way to the left and way to the right.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:11.200
Um, and because that's really all that you could do in this game, uh, they had to switch

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:18.980
up, uh, steering by every time you put an input into the left or right on a D pad is just like

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:22.300
turning you to a certain degree in that direction.

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:26.300
And when you are not pressing anything, the wheels stay there.

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:32.280
And that's kind of like, it's hard to unlearn in most other racing games where if you remove

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:39.220
your input from the, from whatever steering you have, whether it's a wheel in front of

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:48.040
you or an analog stick, um, the, it will usually bring you back to the wheels are straight.

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:54.720
So instead, if you're taking a tight turn, you have to like triple tap on left or not

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:58.680
triple tap, but like sort of ease into a hard left or a hard right.

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:03.740
And then when you need to straighten out again, you have to do the reverse to get back to straight

00:23:03.740 --> 00:23:12.260
wheels. And like, that's sort of, uh, unlearning how to walk in a way or learning how to skip.

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:17.600
It was, it was a weird way that I think that might've affected how bad we were at this game.

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:23.000
Yeah. I mean, definitely. And I remember having that exact thought at first.

