It's one of those funny things in all racing games where like you're always last to go on

00:26:02.480 --> 00:26:05.080
on these things like you have all the information in front of you.

00:26:05.240 --> 00:26:09.060
It's not like, oh, qualify and then find out the times like you just conveniently go last

00:26:09.060 --> 00:26:15.860
or in Gran Turismo games where there aren't qualifying sessions, which please, Polyphony,

00:26:16.040 --> 00:26:17.260
please put those back in.

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:21.960
When there's not qualifying sessions, it's just like you're just conveniently last and the

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:25.940
whole game is just like they also know you're just going to be the fastest car.

00:26:26.060 --> 00:26:28.560
So it's just about racing back to the front.

00:26:28.680 --> 00:26:32.280
And that's like a weird feeling where the qualifying sessions kind of eliminate that.

00:26:32.480 --> 00:26:37.900
But in the qualifying sessions for Michael Andretti's World GP, there are two unique features,

00:26:37.900 --> 00:26:45.880
I thought. One is that once you feel like you've got a lap that's fast enough to qualify at all,

00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:50.940
right? So if it was 140 and you posted a 139 and you're like, oh, I'm just happy to be in the

00:26:50.940 --> 00:26:53.360
race, you can hit the select button at any time.

00:26:53.560 --> 00:26:55.080
It doesn't have to be at the end of a lap or anything.

00:26:55.220 --> 00:27:00.600
You can just hit the select button and it is not necessary to do all five laps.

00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:03.400
You just get to end it right there and slot right in.

00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:08.960
So it's great that it's not this mandatory thing that you have to sit through, watch everybody

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.660
else race. Then you race.

00:27:10.880 --> 00:27:12.080
Then you have to do five laps.

00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:13.660
And then you can finally join the race.

00:27:13.740 --> 00:27:16.200
It's just post a qualifying time and move on.

00:27:16.620 --> 00:27:23.120
However, if you don't qualify at all, if you do your five laps and don't qualify, you have

00:27:23.120 --> 00:27:30.980
to sit out of the race and watch from a different driver's perspective, which like granted, you

00:27:30.980 --> 00:27:33.820
know, we're talking about having a hard time qualifying for the first race.

00:27:33.860 --> 00:27:36.720
So you would just reset the console at that point.

00:27:36.720 --> 00:27:41.640
But if you're like deep into this and you don't qualify for a race, now you just kind

00:27:41.640 --> 00:27:44.760
of going to be like, all right, I guess it's time for a snack.

00:27:45.060 --> 00:27:46.900
Like, well, you could.

00:27:46.900 --> 00:27:52.280
I feel like if you really wanted to play it straight and not cheese the systems, like

00:27:52.280 --> 00:27:54.000
that would be what you do.

00:27:54.140 --> 00:27:57.420
But this game does have a password system.

00:27:57.520 --> 00:28:05.400
So I assume that if you didn't want to waste your time watching the computer race, you could

00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:07.680
just put in the old password and do it again.

00:28:07.900 --> 00:28:13.620
And then inside the race, one thing that's interesting is that there's no direct interaction

00:28:13.620 --> 00:28:15.000
between all the vehicles.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:16.980
The other vehicles kind of act like ghosts.

00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:19.220
Now they do slow you down.

00:28:19.220 --> 00:28:21.420
So do not collide with them by any means.

00:28:21.560 --> 00:28:28.380
But there isn't any sort of crash or ability to take out a computer via malicious means.

00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:32.880
Right, right. You can't like knowingly look at the map and be like, oh, he's right behind me.

00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:37.840
I'm going to like make it so that this way when he gets close, I'll just crash into him

00:28:37.840 --> 00:28:40.020
and, you know, I'm the smarter player or whatever.

00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:40.980
You can't do that.

00:28:40.980 --> 00:28:49.180
But during the race, even though spinning out is like the possibility of probably the worst

00:28:49.180 --> 00:28:52.460
slowdown you can have is spinning out and having to regain speed.

00:28:52.620 --> 00:28:59.800
There's no incident on the course whether your tires are completely blown out or and you

00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:02.960
don't pit or you spin out onto the grass.

00:29:03.120 --> 00:29:04.960
Like nothing can cause a DNF.

00:29:05.560 --> 00:29:08.700
You just have to you just have to keep on racing.

00:29:09.640 --> 00:29:11.400
I mean, I guess that's nice.

00:29:11.780 --> 00:29:19.060
I don't think we it would cause more frustration if you if you took a turn poorly enough.

00:29:19.060 --> 00:29:24.700
And I'm sure we would be the ones to experience this like you just kept like crashing and burning.

00:29:25.020 --> 00:29:27.000
I feel like that'd be even more frustrating.

00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:28.940
After all that time qualifying.

00:29:29.340 --> 00:29:31.480
Yeah. Yeah, absolutely.

00:29:31.940 --> 00:29:33.220
Yeah. So not a complaint for me.

00:29:33.340 --> 00:29:36.220
Just an interesting note of what the game's able to handle.

00:29:36.220 --> 00:29:44.860
And then as far as the remainder of career or Grand Prix mode goes, you for each race, points

00:29:44.860 --> 00:29:47.400
are awarded to the the top four.

00:29:47.860 --> 00:29:49.220
First place gets five.

00:29:49.520 --> 00:29:51.940
Second place, three. Fourth place gets one.

00:29:52.100 --> 00:29:53.560
And fifth place gets none.

00:29:53.780 --> 00:30:00.920
So at the end of the level, a the level being multiple races, it's not just one, but a champion

00:30:00.920 --> 00:30:03.280
is declared based on whoever got the most points.

00:30:03.280 --> 00:30:06.980
So this is this is why like you must always qualify.

00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:12.680
Like you can't afford to like miss a race, not qualify and then not score any points because

00:30:12.680 --> 00:30:15.340
first place is picking up five points.

00:30:15.680 --> 00:30:22.280
And the only way to move forward into level two, three, et cetera, is to be the champion

00:30:22.280 --> 00:30:23.920
of the current level.

00:30:24.300 --> 00:30:27.840
So there's just like there's a lot of contingencies.

00:30:28.040 --> 00:30:30.700
And so thank goodness they have that password system.

00:30:30.700 --> 00:30:37.980
But but like it takes a while to even know where you stand or if you if you even have enough

00:30:37.980 --> 00:30:43.700
points. Right. The difference is the difference is huge between a first and third place finish.

00:30:43.740 --> 00:30:45.760
It's going to take a lot to make up those points.

